      <h1 id="zero-trust-manager-uninstall_{{ context }}" class="group scroll-mt-20">Uninstalling the {"{"}{"{"} zero_trust_full {"}"}{"}"}<a href="#zero-trust-manager-uninstall_{{ context }}" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>To remove the Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager from OpenShift Container Platform, uninstall the Operator and delete its related resources. This process removes the component from your cluster.</p>
      <h2 id="zero-trust-manager-uninstall-console_zero-trust-manager-uninstall" class="group scroll-mt-20">Uninstalling the Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager<a href="#zero-trust-manager-uninstall-console_zero-trust-manager-uninstall" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">To remove the Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager from your cluster, uninstall the Operator using the web console. This helps you clean up resources and delete the service from your environment.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have access to the cluster with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      <li>You have access to the OpenShift Container Platform web console.</li>
      <li>The Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager is installed.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>Log in to the OpenShift Container Platform web console.</li>
      <li>
      Uninstall the Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager.
      <ol>
      <li>Go to <strong>Ecosystem</strong> -&gt; <strong>Installed Operators</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click the <strong>Options</strong> menu next to the <strong>Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager</strong> entry, and then click <strong>Uninstall Operator</strong>.</li>
      <li>In the confirmation dialog, click <strong>Uninstall</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify that the Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager Operator is uninstalled.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get csv -n openshift-zero-trust-workload-identity"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"No resources found in openshift-zero-trust-workload-identity namespace."} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="zero-trust-manager-uninstall-resources_zero-trust-manager-uninstall" class="group scroll-mt-20">Uninstalling Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager resources by using the CLI<a href="#zero-trust-manager-uninstall-resources_zero-trust-manager-uninstall" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Remove Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager resources from your cluster using the CLI. This deletes the remaining operands and definitions to help ensure a clean environment after you uninstall the product.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have access to the cluster with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Uninstall the operands by running each of the following commands:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>SpireOIDCDiscoveryProvider</code> cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete SpireOIDCDiscoveryProvider cluster"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>SpiffeCSIDriver</code> cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete SpiffeCSIDriver cluster -l"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>SpireAgent</code> cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete SpireAgent cluster"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>SpireServer</code> cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete SpireServer cluster"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>ZeroTrustWorkloadIdentityManager</code> cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete ZeroTrustWorkloadIdentityManager cluster"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the persistent volume claim (PVC) by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete pvc -l=app.kubernetes.io/name=spire-server"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the service by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete service -l=app.kubernetes.io/name=zero-trust-workload-identity-manager -n zero-trust-workload-identity-manager"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the namespace by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete ns zero-trust-workload-identity-manager"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the cluster role by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete clusterrole -l=app.kubernetes.io/name=zero-trust-workload-identity-manager"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the admission webhook configuration by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete validatingwebhookconfigurations -l=app.kubernetes.io/name=zero-trust-workload-identity-manager"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the custom resource definitions (CRDs) by running each of the following commands:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Delete the SPIRE Server CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd spireservers.operator.openshift.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the SPIRE Agent CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd spireagents.operator.openshift.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the SPIFFEE CSI Drivers CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd spiffecsidrivers.operator.openshift.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the SPIRE OIDC Discovery Provider CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd spireoidcdiscoveryproviders.operator.openshift.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the SPIRE and SPIFFE cluster federated trust domains CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd clusterfederatedtrustdomains.spire.spiffe.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the cluster SPIFFE IDs CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd clusterspiffeids.spire.spiffe.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the SPIRE and SPIFFE cluster static entries CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd clusterstaticentries.spire.spiffe.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager CRD by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete crd zerotrustworkloadidentitymanagers.operator.openshift.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <p>To verify that the resources have been deleted, replace each <code>oc delete</code> command with <code>oc get</code>, and then run the command. If no resources are returned, the deletion was successful.</p>
